              "<strong>Winfield's Definition:</strong> <em>\"Nuisance as a tort means an unlawful interference with a person's use or enjoyment of land, or of some right over, or in connection with it.\"</em>",
              "<strong>Nuisance vs. Trespass:</strong><br/>• <em>Trespass:</em> Direct, physical entry upon the plaintiff’s land (actionable per se).<br/>• <em>Nuisance:</em> Indirect, consequential interference (e.g., sending smoke, foul smells, unbearable noise, vibrations, or water percolation onto the plaintiff's land). Must prove actual substantial discomfort."
